lution but we've been fighting rbh for  a long time for a number of years for  exactly that that solution but I don't  think it's that easy  and it will be now down to Michael gov  to look at all the implications there  are there's not only the logistical  logistical issues to overcome but  there's a matter of funding taking the  homes back back under Council control  means that the council will need some  funding to um to set up the the systems  to administer and to manage those homes  but it would be ideal we've got some  great counselors in this in this town  um councilor Danny Meredith has been  working alongside us as a campaign for  many years it's just unfortunate that  little Al Arab's death has brought it  under the spotlight and and focus  people's minds on social housing not  just in Rochdale but nationally going to  use his seat inside some of the the  properties run by this Association we've  been hearing first-hand accounts of the  the state of some of those properties  what can be done in the immediate term  to to improve the quality of life for  the people who are living in these  substandard conditions well the first  thing that that they can do is make mold  a category one  um a category one  issue that needs dealing with within one  week and that means setting up the  infrastructure to be able to deal with  it to provide ventilation to provide the  removal of of mold and give people a  decent home which is everybody's right  everybody's a right to expect a clean  dry home to live in and these people  particularly the people on on Freehold  you like I have been around Freehold and  being into some of these disgusting  homes our ab's home was described as not  fit for human habitation and it is  disgusting in 2022 that we have families  living in such circumstances  thanks very much for for joining us  today there's been a very good turnout  here to the uh to the video for young  it's been a terrible shock to this  community although many people say